const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'What is the best Bay Area golf trip for a group of friends?',
    a: 'For a group of 8–20 serious golfers driving from the Bay Area, Graeagle, California is the best option. You get Golf Digest Top 100 Grizzly Ranch, the Nakoma Dragon with its Frank Lloyd Wright clubhouse, and three other championship courses — all within 12 miles of each other. The drive is 3.5 hours on I-80 East. No flights, no coordinating multiple vendors, no group texts about payments. One contract covers tee times, lodging, and dinner reservations. Confirmed before anyone leaves the Bay Area.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I plan a golf trip from the Bay Area?',
    a: 'Tell us your dates, group size, and which courses interest your group. We send a full itinerary — with confirmed tee times, lodging options, and dinner suggestions — within 24 hours. Everyone in your group receives an individual invitation through TripsCaddie, our group coordination platform. Each person registers and pays their own share directly. Whoever organized the trip sets it up once and is done. One contract, one deposit for the group.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can we get a tee time at Grizzly Ranch Golf Club from the Bay Area?',
    a: 'Yes. Grizzly Ranch is not available through GolfNow, Tee Off, or any public booking site. The course prioritizes direct relationships with operators. GolfGraeagle.com holds that relationship and can secure priority tee times for groups that book through us. This is one of the core reasons Bay Area groups book with us rather than trying to coordinate Grizzly Ranch independently.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How far is Graeagle from San Francisco?',
    a: 'Graeagle is approximately 3.5 hours from San Francisco via I-80 East toward Sacramento, then Highway 89 North at Truckee. The drive is straightforward — no mountain passes, no two-lane roads. Most Bay Area groups depart Thursday evening after work or Friday morning before 7am to arrive in time for a 10am tee time.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is Graeagle better than Lake Tahoe for a guys golf trip?',
    a: 'If the trip is primarily about the golf, Graeagle is the better choice. You get a Golf Digest Top 100 course and a Frank Lloyd Wright clubhouse at a fraction of the green fee you would pay in Tahoe. The courses are concentrated within 12 miles. There is no casino floor between you and the first tee in the morning. Tahoe has the Ritz Carlton and Hyatt if brand-name lodging is the priority — Graeagle is for groups where the tee sheet is the priority.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is TripsCaddie and how does it work for a group golf trip?',
    a: 'TripsCaddie is our proprietary group management platform — we built it specifically for golf group coordination. When you book with GolfGraeagle.com, every person in your group receives a personal invitation. They register themselves, pay their own share directly, and receive their tee times and itinerary automatically. There is no one chasing payments, no spreadsheet, no group text asking who has paid. The trip organizer sets it up once. We have run 19+ Graeagle group programs through TripsCaddie. It is included with every booking.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is the best time of year for a Bay Area golf trip to Graeagle?',
    a: 'June through September is peak season — all five courses open, warm days, clear skies. July and August book early, especially for Grizzly Ranch. May and October are the best-kept secrets: courses are emptier, green fees run 15–20% lower, and the temperatures are ideal for golf without summer heat. Season runs May through October depending on snowpack year to year.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How many golfers do you need for a Graeagle group golf trip?',
    a: 'We work with groups of 8 to 20 for the classic Bay Area golf weekend format. Smaller groups (4–7) can also book through us, especially for 2-night programs. Larger groups (20–40) require advance planning across multiple lodging properties and staggered tee times — we have managed those too. Graeagle at its best is an intimate trip: one or two foursomes, everyone knows each other, pace of play stays fast.',
  },
];

